/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS committed: m3-core-rs ships binary wheels, so pinning exact
# dependency versions is required for reproducible builds AND for supply-chain
# scanning (cargo-audit reads Cargo.lock against the RustSec advisory DB).
*.pdb
__pycache__/

# Bench artifacts — local timings, stderr captures, parity JSONs, hardware-
# revealing paths. Per CLAUDE.md, bench data does not ship to public origin.
reports/
embedded_build.log
dist/
crates/*/dist/

# Wheels — built locally, redistributed via CI/release process, not via git.
*.whl

# Local build/staging scratch — these hold host-specific paths (usernames,
# build-box names), build logs, and the wheel-staging tree. Per CLAUDE.md they
# must never reach public origin. Ignore the whole dirs, not just *.whl, so
# build logs / SHA256SUMS / output captures can't be accidentally committed.
ci-wheels/
.scratch/
*.out
CORE_README.md

# Compiled PyO3 extension — platform/Python-specific build artifact dropped by
# `maturin develop` into the source package dir. Like wheels, it is produced
# from source by CI/release, never tracked (would drift from the .rs source and
# is wrong for every other platform/ABI).
crates/m3-core-py/python/m3_core_rs/*.pyd
crates/m3-core-py/python/m3_core_rs/*.so
crates/m3-core-py/python/m3_core_rs/*.dylib


# Per-machine local Claude Code settings — user-specific paths/permissions, never tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
